From a39b66b2f61f9d11ce10d65a54a999364d942755 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:16:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 171/171] hir_typeck: a supertrait's associated type keeps the supertrait's
 name when left opaque

tower 0.5.3 util/boxed_clone.rs:124 (ast-grep 0.45.3), in

    impl<R, T> CloneService<R> for T where T: Service<R> + Send + Clone + 'static {
        fn clone_box(&self) -> Box<dyn CloneService<R, Response = T::Response, ..> + Send> {
            Box::new(self.clone())
        }
    }

    error: Failed to find an impl of CloneService<R> for T with Response = <T as Service<R>>::Response

`Response` is an item of the supertrait `Service`. Expanding
`<T as CloneService<R>>::Response` finds the bound `T: Service<R>`
with no binding for it, and since 0119 (a where-clause bound on a
generic wins over blanket impls) leaves the projection opaque. It left
it under the sub-trait's name, though, so it never compared equal to
`<T as Service<R>>::Response`. Before 0119 the projection went through
the blanket impl, and tower failed earlier anyway.

The opaque projection is now named through the trait that declares the
item, where the bound matched (the `trait_path` from
trait_contains_type, whose assignment to `pe.trait` was commented
out).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index 28b52496..6f399500 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -3036,6 +3036,15 @@ void TraitResolution::expand_associated_types_inplace__UfcsKnown(const Span& sp,
         switch(result_type)
         {
         case ResultType::Opaque: {
+            // The item belongs to a supertrait, where the bound matched: name it through that trait, as the bound
+            // (and the other side of a comparison) does
+            // - tower 0.5.3 util/boxed_clone.rs: in `impl<R, T: Service<R>> CloneService<R> for T`,
+            //   `<T as CloneService<R>>::Response` stayed apart from `<T as Service<R>>::Response` ->
+            //   "Failed to find an impl of CloneService<R> for T with Response = <T as Service<R>>::Response"
+            if( trait_path.m_path != pe.trait.m_path ) {
+                DEBUG("- Item from supertrait " << trait_path);
+                pe.trait = trait_path.clone();
+            }
             DEBUG("Assuming that " << input << " is an opaque name");
             input.data_mut().as_Path().binding = ::HIR::TypePathBinding::make_Opaque({});
             ASSERT_BUG(sp,
